The '''sixth series''' (Season 3 on PBS, or Collection 3 on [[Netflix]] in the US) of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' first aired on 5 August 2015, with twelve contestants competing to be the series 6 winner.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/tvandradio/great-british-bake-off/11741100/season-6-start-date.html |title=When is The Great British Bake Off on? |publisher=Telegraph |date=22 July 2015 |accessdate=22 July 2015}}</ref> [[Mel Giedroyc]] and [[Sue Perkins]] presented the show, and [[Mary Berry (food writer)|Mary Berry]] and [[Paul Hollywood]] returned as judges.{{citation needed|date=April 2020}} The competition was held in the ground of [[Welford Park]], Berkshire for a second year.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/tvandradio/great-british-bake-off/11780930/welford-park-great-british-bake-off.html |title=Welcome to Welford Park: home of The Great British Bake Off |author=Alice Vincent|date=4 August 2015 |work=Daily Telegraph}}</ref> The series was won by [[Nadiya Hussain]], with [[Tamal Ray]] and [[Finalists of The Great British Bake Off (series 1–7)#Ian Cumming|Ian Cumming]] finishing as runners-up.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/tvandradio/great-british-bake-off/11917726/The-Great-British-Bake-Off-2015-the-final-Nadiya-crowned-winner.html|title=The Great British Bake Off 2015: the final – Nadiya crowned winner|date=8 October 2015|work=Daily Telegraphl|accessdate=9 October 2015}}</ref>

The sixth series was broadcast as the third season on [[PBS]] in the [[United States]].

