=== Episode 10: Final ===
In the final signature challenge, the bakers had to make 16 [[iced bun]]s, of which there must be 2 kinds, in 3 hours. In the technical challenge, the judges decided to use one of Paul Hollywood's recipes; the bakers had to bake 6 raspberry-flavoured [[mille-feuille]] with [[fondant icing]] in 2 hours. The recipe involved [[Puff pastry#Variants and distinctions|pastry]] – something all of the bakers had struggled with in Week Six. In the final showstopper, the bakers were given 4 hours to make a classic British cake in a minimum three-layered presentation.{{sticky header}}{{table alignment}}
